    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30333" root="علك" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلَاكٌ</span></b>  <i>A thing that is chewed;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَاكٌ</span></b> 
[and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوكٌ</span></b>  (see 5)]: so in the saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا ذَاقَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلَاكًا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَاكًا</span> [and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوكًا</span>, i. e. <i>He tasted not a
thing that is chewed;</i> meaning, <i>anything</i>]. (K,
TA.) ＝   
